## How you are scored

On the **held-out split, which is not in this workspace**. Your policy and the
ranking origin are run over an identical grid of cells and compared **pairwise**,
and the lift must clear a paired confidence interval.

Two consequences worth internalising:

* **Beating the origin on an easier matchup earns nothing.** Both arms play the
  same opponents, seats and seeds, so the comparison already controls for that.
* **A handful of lucky cells does not clear the interval.** Variance is what the
  interval is measuring. A real improvement has to show up across the grid.

`./run_train_sweep.sh` scores the TRAIN split and writes its artifacts for you to
read. That is feedback, not your score — the gap between your train number and
your held-out number is exactly the overfitting this benchmark exists to find.

## Rules

- The graded evaluator, the roster and the ranking origin live **outside this
  workspace** and are read from there. Editing your copies changes nothing about
  your grade — it only makes your own feedback lie to you.
- Do not attempt to reconstruct the held-out split.
- Add your submission at the path in the table above. It is the only file the
  verifier reads out of this workspace.
